[Page:Defects]
PageContent=#INCLUDE(DefectsContent)

[DefectsContent]
<div class="paragraph">
A player good enough to clear all 100 levels may never get to. Before they do, the
playfield can freeze, or the ball can fall into a loop it cannot leave on its own.
</div>

<table class="default">
<caption>The defects, worst first</caption>
<thead>
<tr>
<th scope="col">Defect</th>
<th scope="col">What breaks</th>
<th scope="col">Cost</th>
<th scope="col">Needs</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><a href="#wedge">Wedge</a></td>
<td>Ball pinned against a golden brick's face; the level cannot clear and the score climbs</td>
<td>Unwinnable</td>
<td>A ball that meets a golden brick's face almost along it</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#shuttle">Shuttle</a></td>
<td>Ball alternates between two golden bricks</td>
<td>Unwinnable</td>
<td>A diagonal ball that reflects at an inside corner of solid cells at each end</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#orbit">Orbit</a></td>
<td>Ball circulates among golden bricks along a path of more than two legs</td>
<td>Unwinnable</td>
<td>Faces and corners of golden bricks and borders that return the ball to its first state</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#skim">Skim</a></td>
<td>Ball skims under the top border and never returns</td>
<td>Unwinnable</td>
<td>Any level</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#scramble">Scramble</a></td>
<td>Playfield freezes while the game plays on underneath</td>
<td>Unplayable</td>
<td>Bat on the right, bottom-left corner clear</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#missed-clear">Missed clear</a></td>
<td>No destructible bricks are left, but the level does not end</td>
<td>Level held open</td>
<td>A ball that hits golden bricks after the last destructible brick breaks</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#dud">Dud</a></td>
<td>A bomb in another bomb's blast shatters and never detonates</td>
<td>Lost prize</td>
<td>Two bombs next to each other</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#orb-drift">Orb drift</a></td>
<td>Orb wears other inhabitants' sprites while it returns the ball</td>
<td>Cosmetic</td>
<td>An orb that catches the ball</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#speck">Speck</a></td>
<td>A stray speck sits inside the visor's sprite</td>
<td>Cosmetic</td>
<td>Any key the ROM accepts during the front end</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#fire-gate">Fire gate</a></td>
<td>The missile launch ignores the fire key while the bat is frozen or stung, or moves under inertia</td>
<td>Missile ignored or misfired</td>
<td>A missile bat armed while the bat is frozen or stung, or moves under inertia</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><a href="#ufo">UFO</a></td>
<td>The UFO never appears</td>
<td>None in play</td>
<td>Any level</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>

<h2 class="ref-section" id="reflection-reset">How the ball gets stuck</h2>

<div class="paragraph">
Wedge, shuttle, orbit and skim trap the ball in a path it cannot leave. The ball
moves in sub-pixel steps. Each axis moves one pixel only when its own count
#R$A4F6(fills up). Every bounce #R$A2D8(empties both counts) and leaves the
ball where it is. A ball that bounces before its slow axis moves a pixel
therefore travels on one axis only.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
A bounce depends only on the ball's heading and on what it hits. A ball that comes
back to a place at a heading it had there before repeats its path for good. The
#R$8C26(anti-stuck nudge) turns ball A around after 30 frames within 16 pixels of where it was on both axes.
The next bounce undoes the turn, because a heading and its opposite
#R$A424(leave a surface at the same heading).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
A trapped ball never returns to the bat. Destructible bricks off its path stay out
of reach. The level cannot clear while any remain. With none left, the level
<a href="#missed-clear">ends late</a>.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="wedge">Wedge</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The ball sticks to a golden brick.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/wedge.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
The ball meets the face of a golden brick almost along the face. It bounces off
the face each time it probes ahead, and never moves away from it.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Each bounce #R$A99B(scores). Only a #R$A777(bat bounce) resets the combo. The
score climbs without end.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="shuttle">Shuttle</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The ball runs back and forth between two golden bricks.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/shuttle.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
A diagonal ball meets an inside corner of golden bricks, where the cell beside it
and the cell ahead of it both block. A corner sends a diagonal ball
#R$A674(straight back along its line). With such a corner at each end, the ball runs between
them for good.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="orbit">Orbit</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The ball circles among golden bricks.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/orbit.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
The ball bounces among golden bricks and borders along a path of three or more
legs. It comes back to where it started at the heading it started with. It then
repeats the path for good. Nothing on the path ever changes.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="skim">Skim</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The ball never leaves the top border.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/skim.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
The ball runs along just under the top border at a heading close to the
horizontal. Each time it probes ahead, it also tests the border cell above it,
finds it solid and #R$A343(bounces). The bounce is silent and #R$A299(scores nothing).
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="scramble">Scramble</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The playfield freezes.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/scramble.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
Play with the bat on the right, so the wall runs down the left edge. Clear the
bricks from the bottom-left corner and let the ball reach the corner cell.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The game redraws only the cells whose #R$FB00(dirty counter) is set. A
terminator ends the scan. The terminator sits in the bottom-left corner cell. That
cell never changes in normal play. A ball #R$BAF2(drawn there) overwrites the
terminator.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
Without the terminator, the #R$BB38(redraw) runs past the end of the dirty counters. It sprays
graphics over memory. Bands of the screen change color. The redraw never draws
parts of the playfield again. Play and the score go on underneath. The damage lasts
until the #R$8BD0(next level starts).
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="missed-clear">Missed clear</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">Every destructible brick is gone, but the level plays on.</p>
</hgroup>

<video src="videos/defects/missed-clear.mp4" width="512" height="384" controls playsinline preload="metadata"></video>

<div class="paragraph">
A level ends when every brick slot is empty or holds a golden brick at rest. The #R$AF20(check for this)
skips a golden brick only when it shows its plain face. A golden brick flashes when the ball
hits it. It also #R$B0BF(twinkles at random). In either case the check takes it for
a brick still to break.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The level ends at the first check that finds every golden brick at rest. A ball
that bounces among golden bricks therefore pushes the end back, for as long as it
stays there.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="dud">Dud</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">A bomb in the blast never goes off.</p>
</hgroup>

<div class="paragraph">
<div class="inset">#UDGARRAY2,7,3,tindex=1,alpha=0($DBE8,$46;$DBF0,$44;$DBD8,$46;$DC00,$44;$DBE8,$46;$DBF0,$44;$DBD8,$46;$DC00,$44)(two_bombs)</div>
When two bombs lie next to each other and the ball takes one, its #R$B21D(blast) clears
the eight bricks around it. The other bomb shatters like a plain brick and never
detonates.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="orb-drift">Orb drift</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The orb wears the wrong sprites.</p>
</hgroup>

<div class="paragraph">
An #R$D05B(orb) that catches the ball chews it, then spits it out, and the ball
slides back toward the bat. On the way its animation runs past its last frame and never stops. The orb
then wears frames of the comet and then of the hive.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The drift ends when the ball reaches the bat's losing edge. There the player
#R$9FFF(loses the ball).
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="speck">Speck</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">A stray speck sits in the visor's sprite.</p>
</hgroup>

<div class="paragraph">
A key pressed while the front end is on screen leaves a speck in the visor's
first frame. It stays until the player resets the machine.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
The ROM stores the last key it accepts in LAST-K. The game keeps a byte of the
#R$5C00(visor's sprite) at the same address. It never copies the sprite in
again.
</div>

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="fire-gate">Fire gate</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The fire test reads the wrong byte.</p>
</hgroup>

<div class="paragraph">
The #R$9A8D(missile launch) tests fire in a value it does not choose itself.
Under direct control, and under the inertia option while the bat stands still,
that value is the #R$BC23(controls).
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
While the bat moves under the inertia option, it is a step from the
#R$9B67(inertia speed ramp). During the bat freeze, it is the
#R$5B92(freeze timer). Neither ever holds the fire bit, so the missile does not
launch.
</div>

<div class="paragraph">
During the bee's sting, it is whatever the
#R$9CB3(object manager) used last. The launch then follows that value, not the fire
key.
</div>

#UDGARRAY2,7,3,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E521,,2;$E520,,2;$E531,,2;$E530,,2)(*ufo_1)
#UDGARRAY2,7,3,2,tindex=1,alpha=0($E541,,2;$E540,,2;$E551,,2;$E550,,2)(*ufo_2)

<hgroup class="ref-head">
<h2 class="ref-section" id="ufo">UFO</h2>
<p class="ref-deck">The UFO never spawns.</p>
</hgroup>

<div class="paragraph">
<div class="inset">#FRAMES(ufo_1,8;ufo_2,8)(ufo)</div>
The game carries a whole UFO: two sprite frames, an animation and a
#R$CDE8(behavior handler). Nothing spawns it, so it never appears in play.
</div>
